 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in Senate",
   "date": "2023-10-19",
   "text": "Medical Debt Relief Act of 2023\nThis bill prohibits consumer reporting agencies from including medical debt on a consumer report (i.e., credit report). In addition, the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau must amend regulations to prohibit creditors from obtaining or using medical debt information when considering whether to extend credit to a consumer."
  }
